@startuml

' The end-to-end flow that turns a folder of images into reviewable duplicate groups
' The per-pair ZNCC score is computed on the GPU; the clustering and keeper selection
' run on the CPU over the resulting similarity matrix

title ImgLabs — Duplicate Detection Pipeline

skinparam shadowing false

start
:Import images;
:Resample to a common canvas\n(min width & height across the set);
:Build the similarity matrix\n(all pairs, lower triangle only — ZNCC is symmetric);
note right
  Each pair is scored on the GPU:
  grayscale -> mean -> subtract-mean ->
  square -> sum -> dot product
end note
:Cluster with Union-Find\n(connect every pair scoring >= threshold);
:Choose one keeper per cluster\n(medoid: highest average similarity);
:Render duplicate groups\n(DuplicateView, keep vs. remove);
stop

@enduml
